WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.097
Dilations, scaled copies, and slope.

2
00:00:02.097 --> 00:00:08.970
These sound like three different ideas, but they are really one idea: stretching a picture without changing its shape.

3
00:00:09.917 --> 00:00:13.175
Here is a triangle with sides three, four, and five.

4
00:00:13.175 --> 00:00:18.249
Multiply every side by the same number, say two, and you get six, eight, and ten.

5
00:00:18.249 --> 00:00:22.134
That is a scaled copy, and the number two is the scale factor.

6
00:00:22.134 --> 00:00:24.577
Notice the angles do not change at all.

7
00:00:24.917 --> 00:00:30.116
But if we stretch the triangle only sideways, the angles change and the shape gets distorted.

8
00:00:30.116 --> 00:00:31.569
That is not a scaled copy.

9
00:00:31.569 --> 00:00:34.756
Every length must be multiplied by the same scale factor.

10
00:00:35.700 --> 00:00:40.369
A dilation makes a scaled copy using one special point, called the center of dilation.

11
00:00:40.369 --> 00:00:42.921
Draw a ray from the center through each corner.

12
00:00:42.921 --> 00:00:47.156
With a scale factor of two, each new point lands twice as far from the center.

13
00:00:47.500 --> 00:00:52.642
With a scale factor of one half, each point lands half as far away, so the copy shrinks.

14
00:00:52.642 --> 00:00:55.388
A scale factor bigger than one makes it bigger.

15
00:00:55.388 --> 00:00:57.608
Between zero and one makes it smaller.

16
00:00:57.608 --> 00:01:00.529
And a scale factor of exactly one changes nothing.

17
00:01:01.467 --> 00:01:08.842
On a coordinate grid, when the center of dilation is the origin, just multiply both coordinates by the scale factor.

18
00:01:08.842 --> 00:01:13.674
The point two, one, dilated by a scale factor of three, lands at six, three.

19
00:01:14.617 --> 00:01:15.260
Now, slope.

20
00:01:15.260 --> 00:01:18.065
Draw a line, and tuck a right triangle under it.

21
00:01:18.065 --> 00:01:21.923
The slope is the vertical change divided by the horizontal change.

22
00:01:21.923 --> 00:01:26.014
Here the rise is two and the run is three, so the slope is two thirds.

23
00:01:26.350 --> 00:01:27.901
Here is the beautiful part.

24
00:01:27.901 --> 00:01:33.989
Dilate that slope triangle from a point on the line, and you get a bigger slope triangle on the same line.

25
00:01:33.989 --> 00:01:35.080
Rise four, run six.

26
00:01:35.080 --> 00:01:36.918
Four sixths is still two thirds.

27
00:01:36.918 --> 00:01:42.949
Every slope triangle on a line is a scaled copy of the others, and that is why a line has just one slope.

28
00:01:43.283 --> 00:01:48.134
If the line goes down as you move to the right, the rise is negative, so the slope is negative.

29
00:01:49.083 --> 00:01:49.783
So remember.

30
00:01:49.783 --> 00:01:52.174
The scale factor multiplies every length.

31
00:01:52.174 --> 00:01:55.323
The center of dilation is where the stretching starts.

32
00:01:55.323 --> 00:01:58.706
And slope is rise over run, the same everywhere on a line.

33
00:01:58.706 --> 00:02:00.047
Good luck on your test!
